1
00:00:07,426 --> 00:00:16,337
-==www.RagBear.com==- 是, 首相  第1季第5集

2
00:00:17,615 --> 00:00:25,384
<font color="#4096d1">本字幕仅供学习交流，严禁用于商业用途

3
00:00:25,384 --> 00:00:31,970
<font color="#4096d1">-=破烂熊字幕组=- 翻译&校对&时间轴: tpring

4
00:00:35,741 --> 00:00:39,130
休戚相关

5
00:00:39,895 --> 00:00:42,489
你好啊 亲爱的 内阁会议顺利吗?
Hello, darling. Good Cabinet meeting?

6
00:00:42,655 --> 00:00:45,647
内阁会议顺利吗 亲爱的?
Hmm. Good Cabinet meeting, darling?

7
00:00:45,815 --> 00:00:49,569
我要三份威士忌      这么惨 怎么啦?
I want a triple Scotch! As bad as that? Why?

8
00:00:50,775 --> 00:00:56,964
经济危机比预期严重得多 内阁各部门都得削减开支
The crisis is worse than we thought. the Cabinet must make cuts.

9
00:00:57,175 --> 00:01:01,612
伯纳 来杯威士忌吗?      好的 请给大杯行吗?
Bernard, would you like a Scotch? Yes, a large one, please.

10
00:01:00,735 --> 00:01:01,803
也来三份
Another triple

11
00:01:01,803 --> 00:01:04,966
伯纳 汉弗莱该预料到这个 警告我
Humphrey should have seen this coming.

12
00:01:05,175 --> 00:01:09,373
我认为他不懂经济 首相 他念的古典文学
I don't think he understands Economics. He did read Classics.

13
00:01:09,535 --> 00:01:11,924
弗兰克爵士呢? 他是财政部首脑
Sir Frank is head of the Treasury.

14
00:01:12,135 --> 00:01:17,084
恐怕他更不可能懂经济 他是个经济学家
greater disadvantage in understanding Economics. He's an economist.

15
00:01:17,295 --> 00:01:20,139
经济危机了 内阁大臣料不到要削减经费吗?
Can't they see there's got to be cuts?

16
00:01:20,139 --> 00:01:22,728
都料到在别的部门 轮不到他们自己
In other departments, not in their own!

17
00:01:22,728 --> 00:01:24,889
今天早晨你下限制令啦?
So you ordered a clampdown?

18
00:01:25,055 --> 00:01:30,083
我没权力下令 我不过是个首相      可你负全责啊
I can't do that. I'm only the Prime Minister. But you're in charge.

19
00:01:30,295 --> 00:01:34,254
不 领导人只能听别人意见 服从多数 这是民主
A leader can only lead by consent, consensus. That's democracy.

20
00:01:34,455 --> 00:01:37,447
你不负责 那到底谁负责?      没人负责
So who IS in charge? Nobody, really.

21
00:01:37,615 --> 00:01:41,893
这样好吗?      肯定好 这就是民主的目的
Is that good? It must be. That's what democracy is about.

22
00:01:42,095 --> 00:01:45,759
麻烦的是 下午还有个议员代表团来找我
And I've got a deputation of MPs coming

23
00:01:45,759 --> 00:01:48,485
商量我答应给他们加薪的事
to see me about a pay rise I promised them.

24
00:01:48,485 --> 00:01:52,010
你要怎么说?      我会说我非常同情 其实我没有
What will you say? That I deeply sympathise. I don't.

25
00:01:52,175 --> 00:01:54,564
加薪是他们应得的 其实不是
That they fully deserve it. Not true.

26
00:01:54,735 --> 00:01:59,525
只要危机过去我打算当作头等大事来抓 其实我没这打算
my first priority as soon as the crisis is over. I shan't.

27
00:01:59,695 --> 00:02:03,688
如果他们投票给自己大幅加薪 然后宣布没钱给别人加
If they vote themselves a whacking great pay rise,

28
00:02:03,855 --> 00:02:08,087
也不会给议会增光添彩 确实不会
it doesn't do very much for the dignity of Parliament. It doesn't.

29
00:02:08,295 --> 00:02:13,289
他们真的报酬过低吗?      报酬过低?后座议员?亲爱的
Are they underpaid? Underpaid?! Backbench MPs? Darling...

30
00:02:13,495 --> 00:02:16,487
议员是个名利双收的顶级肥差
Being an MP is a vast, subsidised ego trip.

31
00:02:16,655 --> 00:02:22,571
没有资质考核 没有固定时数 没有评价标准
You need no qualifications, no compulsory hours of work, no performance standards.

32
00:02:23,575 --> 00:02:28,603
用舒适的房间和美食养活一帮自大狂和无事忙
A warm room and meals for a bunch of windbags and busybodies

33
00:02:29,615 --> 00:02:32,364
他们突然发现人们把他们当回事了
who suddenly find people taking them seriously

34
00:02:32,364 --> 00:02:34,445
因为名字后面加了"议员"两个字
because they've got ''MP'' after their names!

35
00:02:34,775 --> 00:02:39,565
他们怎么会报酬过低? 每个位置有200人申请呢
there's about 200 applicants for every vacancy?

36
00:02:39,735 --> 00:02:44,331
就算要交钱上任 每个位置还能卖20次
You could fill every seat 20 times if they paid to do the job!

37
00:02:44,535 --> 00:02:47,129
你5年前还是后座议员呢
You were a backbench MP only 5 years ago.

38
00:02:47,295 --> 00:02:49,684
我是特例
I was the exception.

39
00:02:49,855 --> 00:02:52,449
我是精华 我升到顶峰了
I was the cream. I rose to the top.

40
00:02:55,055 --> 00:02:58,604
你觉得这说法能压住他们吗?      谁知道
Do you think you'll shut them up? Who knows?

41
00:02:58,815 --> 00:03:04,287
可公众绝不会答应议员涨工资 而护士和教师做削减
The public will never stand when cut back on nurses and teachers.

42
00:03:04,495 --> 00:03:07,248
护士和教师 这问题可严重多了
Oh, that's a much more serious problem.

43
00:03:07,455 --> 00:03:10,416
不 亲爱的 差远了 护士和教师
No, darling, much LESS serious. They

44
00:03:10,416 --> 00:03:12,209
不到下次大选不能投票反对我
can't vote against me till the next election.

45
00:03:12,415 --> 00:03:15,213
后座议员今晚10点就能投我的反对票
Backbenchers can do it at 10 o'clock tonight.

46
00:03:17,575 --> 00:03:20,487
汉弗莱 我刚跟议员们开了个很激烈的会
Humphrey, I've just had a very stormy meeting with my backbenchers!

47
00:03:20,655 --> 00:03:24,648
真遗憾      要是给我点预警 我能先把他们缓和下来
I'm so sorry. If I had warning, I'd have softened them up.

48
00:03:24,815 --> 00:03:29,206
可内阁会议前夜文件才送到      是吗 首相 真令人遗憾
Papers only arrived the night before Cabinet! Most regrettable.

49
00:03:29,415 --> 00:03:35,047
怪你 汉弗莱 你是内阁秘书 你得负责让文件早点送来
You must insist that we get papers circulated earlier.

50
00:03:35,255 --> 00:03:40,045
唉 恐怕文件还没撰写 送来就有很大困难
grave problems in circulating papers before they are written.

51
00:03:41,375 --> 00:03:43,445
怎么突然闹危机 财政部料到了吧?
Why the sudden crisis?

52
00:03:43,655 --> 00:03:47,547
首相 我不是财政部常任秘书 您得问弗兰克爵士
Prime Minister, you must ask Sir Frank.

53
00:03:47,547 --> 00:03:49,116
弗兰克爵士会怎么说?
What would Sir Frank say?

54
00:03:49,116 --> 00:03:51,603
轮不到鄙人这样卑微的凡人
It is not for a humble mortal such as I

55
00:03:51,775 --> 00:03:56,565
对伟人们复杂深远的谋略妄加揣测
to speculate on the complex and deliberations of the mighty,

56
00:03:56,735 --> 00:03:59,247
但总的来说 弗兰克爵士大概认为
but, in general, I think Sir Frank believes that

57
00:03:59,247 --> 00:04:01,310
如果财政部觉得有必要采取某一行动
if the Treasury knows something must be done,

58
00:04:01,310 --> 00:04:04,687
内阁不该有太多时间来考虑它
the Cabinet shouldn't have time to think about it..

59
00:04:04,895 --> 00:04:06,294
太不像话了
Outrageous!

60
00:04:06,495 --> 00:04:11,285
的确 此所谓财政部政策      如果内阁有问题呢?
It's known as Treasury policy. Suppose the Cabinet has questions?

61
00:04:11,495 --> 00:04:16,250
我想他认为 就算财政部难得地理解了问题
on the rare occasions when the Treasury understands the questions,

62
00:04:16,415 --> 00:04:19,407
内阁也不会理解答复
the Cabinet doesn't understand the answers.

63
00:04:19,615 --> 00:04:22,607
你支持这个看法吗?      我吗 首相
Do you subscribe to that view? I, Prime Minister,

64
00:04:22,775 --> 00:04:26,006
我只想尽力达成首相和内阁的愿望
I merely try to carry out your wishes.

65
00:04:26,215 --> 00:04:31,005
我希望今后一切文件在内阁会议前48小时送到
all Cabinet papers be circulated at least 48 hours in advance.

66
00:04:31,175 --> 00:04:34,167
告诉弗兰克爵士好吗?     好 当然
Would you tell Sir Frank? Yes, of course.

67
00:04:34,335 --> 00:04:37,930
我这就去请求他接见 谢谢 首相
I shall seek an audience with him at once. Thank you.

68
00:04:39,695 --> 00:04:44,086
弗兰克以为他是谁? 至少小汉还有自知之明
Who does Frank think he is? At least Old Humpy knows his place.

69
00:04:45,255 --> 00:04:50,534
他真忠诚 居然告诉我真相 他们不是总抱成一团的吗
It was very loyal of him to tell me the truth.

70
00:04:50,735 --> 00:04:54,457
我想他很担心您提出的 让弗兰克爵士取代他
He's rather anxious because of your threat to make Sir Frank

71
00:04:54,457 --> 00:04:56,653
做公务员首脑的事
head of the home Civil Service.

72
00:04:56,653 --> 00:05:00,528
对啊 不知道我是把这件事解决掉呢
Of course. I wonder if I should do something about that.

73
00:05:00,695 --> 00:05:05,371
还是让他俩都提心吊胆的比较有利
Or if to keeping them both in suspense.

74
00:05:05,575 --> 00:05:09,409
首相 您会得到一个紧张的内阁秘书 您乐意吗?
You gain an anxious Cabinet Secretary. Is that what you want?

75
00:05:13,695 --> 00:05:16,084
他不仅是不满意削减的事 弗兰克
He wasn't just unhappy about the cuts, Frank.

76
00:05:16,255 --> 00:05:20,567
他最不满意的是你的文件那么晚才送到
He was unhappy about your papers arriving at such short notice.

77
00:05:20,775 --> 00:05:24,370
你跟他解释了这是因为美国突然调整利率吧
I hope you explained it was because of America's policy change.

78
00:05:24,535 --> 00:05:27,527
亲爱的弗兰克 我对你大加维护
My dear Frank, I defended you gallantly,

79
00:05:29,055 --> 00:05:32,525
让首相对真正原因没有一点怀疑
leaving the Prime Minister in no doubt as to the real cause.

80
00:05:32,735 --> 00:05:35,329
那就好 多谢
Oh, good. Thanks.

81
00:05:36,735 --> 00:05:39,124
我需要他的支持      为什么?
I'll need his goodwill. Why?

82
00:05:39,335 --> 00:05:43,726
显然 因为经济危机 我们得实施些薪酬限制政策
We shall obviously have to bring in some form of pay restraint.

83
00:05:43,895 --> 00:05:48,491
问题是 如果拒绝给议员加薪
The problem is, the MPs are being denied their pay rise

84
00:05:48,655 --> 00:05:52,489
正赶上我们提出公务员加薪计划...
just as we bring forward the proposed Civil Service pay rise.

85
00:05:52,695 --> 00:05:55,084
这就尴尬了      对
Ah. That's an awkward one. Yes.

86
00:05:55,255 --> 00:05:59,692
当然 人并不在乎个人利益      当然不
One isn't interested for oneself... Of course not.

87
00:05:59,895 --> 00:06:04,286
但人总要为下级同僚们着想      真讽刺 对吧 弗兰克?
But one does owe it to one's junior colleagues. Ironic, isn't it

88
00:06:04,455 --> 00:06:09,449
为他们办事 我们也不得不加薪 我们明明不在乎的
Trying to help them involves raising our own salaries

89
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:14,249
还要被人骂作是营私自肥
And then we get accused of feathering our own nests!

90
00:06:14,455 --> 00:06:17,094
这也是我们不得不担的罪名
That's just another cross we have to bear.

91
00:06:17,295 --> 00:06:19,855
对 嫉妒 纯粹是嫉妒
Yes. Envy, pure envy.

92
00:06:21,095 --> 00:06:25,566
你得趁薪酬限制启动前 赶紧提出加薪计划
You'd better get that proposal in before the pay restraint begins.

93
00:06:25,775 --> 00:06:28,164
就在下周四内阁会议前夜
The night before next Thursday's Cabinet.

94
00:06:28,335 --> 00:06:32,328
我们不能给大臣们两天时间
We can't let Ministers spend two days talking about it.

95
00:06:32,495 --> 00:06:35,089
跟政治顾问和议员讨论 他们会提出各种愚蠢的反对意见
They'll come up with stupid objections!

96
00:06:35,295 --> 00:06:37,934
一直把它压到薪酬限制启动
And try to delay it until the pay restraint.

97
00:06:38,135 --> 00:06:42,128
你真的觉得可以跳过两周内阁议程?
Do you think it's all right to bounce the Cabinet running?

98
00:06:42,295 --> 00:06:46,288
没别的办法      我在想 汉弗莱
No alternative. I-I-I was thinking, Humphrey.

99
00:06:47,295 --> 00:06:52,323
也许计划由我们两个共同提出比较稳妥
Perhaps it would be better if the proposal came from both of us.

100
00:06:52,495 --> 00:06:57,205
我们两个?      我们毕竟是公务员的联合领导嘛
Both of us? Well, we are joint heads of the Civil Service.

101
00:06:57,415 --> 00:07:00,327
照我理解不是 弗兰克
Not as I understand it, Frank.

102
00:07:00,535 --> 00:07:04,574
我认为 实际上是的      我认为实际上不是
Oh, I think so, effectively. I think not, effectively.

103
00:07:04,775 --> 00:07:08,848
我管财政方面 你管体制
I look after the financial side and you the establishment side.

104
00:07:09,055 --> 00:07:14,573
可弗兰克 恕我直言 内阁秘书理应被赋予公务员领导权
the Cabinet Secretary is the de jure head of the Civil Service.

105
00:07:14,775 --> 00:07:19,565
恕我直言 汉弗莱 内阁秘书和财政部常任秘书
the Cabinet Secretary and the Permanent Secretary to the Treasury

106
00:07:19,735 --> 00:07:22,295
实务上是在共同领导公务员
are de facto joint heads of the Civil Service.

107
00:07:22,495 --> 00:07:27,091
就算是 弗兰克 我们不能一起提
Be that as it may, Frank, we can't put up the proposal together.

108
00:07:27,255 --> 00:07:29,644
我得保持冷漠和公正
I must remain aloof and judicial.

109
00:07:29,815 --> 00:07:35,208
得由你来发动 经过缜密思考 我再站到你这边来
After weighty consideration, I will come down on your side.

110
00:07:37,335 --> 00:07:39,974
好吧 还有件事
All right. One other point...

111
00:07:40,175 --> 00:07:43,611
显然 我们不能让内阁来裁定
We don't want Cabinet to adjudicate on this.

112
00:07:43,815 --> 00:07:48,013
对 得成立中立委员会审查      谁来做主席?
They must refer it to an impartial committee. Who should chair it?

113
00:07:48,175 --> 00:07:51,963
韦尔斯教授如何?      那个昏聩的老傻瓜?
What about Professor Welsh? That silly old buffer?!

114
00:07:52,175 --> 00:07:54,484
那个昏聩的老傻瓜      为什么?
That silly old buffer. Why?

115
00:07:54,695 --> 00:07:59,689
他要我提名他做大学补助委员会主席
He's asked to be the chairman of the University Grants Committee.

116
00:07:59,855 --> 00:08:04,451
他极其想要那职位 他会理解我们的要求
desperate for the job, so he'll understand what's required of him.

117
00:08:04,655 --> 00:08:07,453
真是明智之选
What an excellent choice.

118
00:08:07,615 --> 00:08:10,004
汉弗莱 我太震惊了
Humphrey, I'm astonished.

119
00:08:10,175 --> 00:08:14,965
财政部刚因为经济危机砍掉了一半开支计划
The Treasury has just cancelled half our spending plans

120
00:08:15,135 --> 00:08:20,573
现在他们居然有胆提出公务员加薪计划
and now they put forward a plan for a Civil Service pay rise!

121
00:08:20,775 --> 00:08:23,164
你还想让它跳过内阁会议
And you're bouncing it through Cabinet!

122
00:08:23,335 --> 00:08:27,143
我说了要所有文件提前48小时送到
I wanted all papers circulated 48 hours in advance.

123
00:08:27,143 --> 00:08:28,870
你觉得我纯粹是白痴吗?
Do you think I'm a complete idiot?

124
00:08:32,095 --> 00:08:35,167
首相 我没权利为弗兰克爵士辩护
It is not for me to speak for Sir Frank.

125
00:08:35,375 --> 00:08:39,846
我要你为自己辩护 你是内阁秘书 也是公务员的领导
Speak for yourself. You're head of the Civil Service.

126
00:08:40,055 --> 00:08:44,765
我是吗? 真让人欣慰      眼下是
Am I indeed? How gratifying! For the moment.

127
00:08:44,975 --> 00:08:49,366
可首相 作为内阁秘书 我也急于削减公共开支
As Cabinet Secretary, I am most eager to reduce public spending,

128
00:08:49,535 --> 00:08:54,529
但作为公务员领导 我得对眼前的行政危机负责
as head of the Service I'm responsible for dangers administratively

129
00:08:54,695 --> 00:08:57,289
如果加薪不能尽快通过的话
if a pay rise does not come through very soon.

130
00:08:57,289 --> 00:09:00,585
我真的很难办 您看 我顶着两个头衔
It's so difficult for me. I'm wearing two hats.

131
00:09:00,695 --> 00:09:03,163
这倒是 你确实很难应付吧?
Yes, isn't that rather awkward for you?

132
00:09:04,015 --> 00:09:06,609
不会 如果有两副头脑的话
Not if one is in two minds.

133
00:09:06,815 --> 00:09:09,090
或者有两副面孔
Or has two faces.

134
00:09:13,375 --> 00:09:15,764
要不要我给你解除一个?
Perhaps I should relieve you of one of them?

135
00:09:15,975 --> 00:09:19,854
不用不用 我非常乐意有两个      面孔?
Oh, no, no, no. I'm perfectly happy with both. Faces?

136
00:09:20,055 --> 00:09:22,171
头衔
Hats!

137
00:09:22,375 --> 00:09:27,768
您看 首相 问题在于士气低下会导致罢工
the problem is that low morale will lead to the danger of a strike.

138
00:09:27,935 --> 00:09:31,928
想想社会服务业电脑员罢工的后果吧
Think of the effect of that on the social services.

139
00:09:32,095 --> 00:09:35,883
再说 我们的招募已经有困难了
And we are already experiencing difficulties in recruitment.

140
00:09:36,095 --> 00:09:40,771
每个职位有10个人申请吧?      对 可申请者素质非常低下
10 applicants for every vacancy? very low quality.

141
00:09:40,935 --> 00:09:46,328
很少人拿一等学位 大多数都只有二等乙级
With very few First Class degrees. Most have Lower Seconds.

142
00:09:47,575 --> 00:09:49,770
我拿的三等
I got a Third.

143
00:09:51,135 --> 00:09:55,526
这对首相足够了 汉弗莱爵士是说公务员
That's all right for PM. Sir Humphrey means civil servants.

144
00:09:55,735 --> 00:10:00,729
重点是 我想批也批不了 后座议员的威胁还没解除呢
The point is There's already a backbench revolt looming.

145
00:10:00,895 --> 00:10:05,730
议员们绝不会同意给公务员加薪 内阁也会反对
MPs will never agree to a pay rise for civil servants.

146
00:10:05,935 --> 00:10:10,884
我能否建议只请内阁过目一下计划?
ask the Cabinet merely to agree to look at the application?

147
00:10:11,055 --> 00:10:15,446
然后把它交给独立小组 详察细节
Then we'll put the matter before an independent group of assessors.

148
00:10:15,655 --> 00:10:20,649
谁来主持评审?      我有个完美的人选
Who would lead these assessors? There's a very good man

149
00:10:20,815 --> 00:10:24,524
韦尔斯教授 非常可靠 非常明智 非常慎重
Professor Welsh. Very sound, very sensible, very careful.

150
00:10:24,735 --> 00:10:27,124
我听说他是个昏聩的老傻瓜
I heard he was a silly old buffer.

151
00:10:27,335 --> 00:10:31,328
真难以想象什么人会说出这种话
I can't imagine who could possibly say such a thing!

152
00:10:33,135 --> 00:10:36,286
由于公务员中最高的两个职位负担最重
Since the most senior grades of the service bear the heat

153
00:10:36,455 --> 00:10:39,049
他们加薪的幅度也最大
they should receive the greatest increase.

154
00:10:39,215 --> 00:10:41,604
我觉得很公平
Seems very fair to me.

155
00:10:41,775 --> 00:10:45,563
这就是预期幅度      好
So this would be the scale. Right.

156
00:10:45,775 --> 00:10:49,734
对了 我可没看过      当然没有 太不合适了
I haven't seen this, by the way. Of course not. Most improper.

157
00:10:49,935 --> 00:10:55,532
对 好吧 副秘书长加了不少啊
they're very significant increases for Under Secretaries,

158
00:10:55,695 --> 00:10:58,084
常务副秘书长也是
Deputy Secretaries and, um,

159
00:10:59,095 --> 00:11:01,655
而我们中最...
those of us who, um...

160
00:11:01,855 --> 00:11:03,652
正是
Exactly.

161
00:11:03,815 --> 00:11:06,204
大约43%
About 43%.

162
00:11:07,095 --> 00:11:10,883
哎呀      不比我们应得的多
Alas. But no more than we've earned.

163
00:11:11,055 --> 00:11:13,489
这份文件不是用来提交的吧
I take it this paper is not for submission.

164
00:11:13,695 --> 00:11:18,086
亲爱的汉弗莱 这才是要提交的文件
My dear Humphrey, those are the submission papers.

165
00:11:20,495 --> 00:11:22,884
哦 对了
Oh, yes.

166
00:11:24,095 --> 00:11:28,327
这才到附录K      抱歉 后面还有6份
It only goes up to Appendix K. Sorry. Six more to follow.

167
00:11:28,535 --> 00:11:31,925
哦 那他们就没有读完的危险了
Oh! No danger of their wading through all those.

168
00:11:32,095 --> 00:11:35,326
给内阁的一页摘要呢?
Where's the one-page summary for the Cabinet?

169
00:11:35,535 --> 00:11:37,924
傻瓜版?
The Janet and John bit?

170
00:11:38,135 --> 00:11:40,524
在这里
Here it is.

171
00:11:40,695 --> 00:11:45,485
跟上次差不多 与工业职位对照表
It's more or less the same as last time.

172
00:11:45,655 --> 00:11:50,775
和什么人的报酬对照?      当然是英国石油和IBM的董事
On whose salary are the comparisons based? The directors of BP

173
00:11:50,975 --> 00:11:56,208
不会被指为过高和非典型吧?
You don't think that might be challenged as untypical?

174
00:11:56,415 --> 00:12:01,409
不会 我们当然不提名字 只叫他们"典型工业公司"
we don't mention them by name. Just ''typical industrial firms''.

175
00:12:01,575 --> 00:12:06,330
然后我们提出我们的加薪例子 从最低阶开始
Then we take our own examples of increases from the lowest point

176
00:12:06,535 --> 00:12:11,734
照老规矩      主要个体例子附在后面
As before. Principal examples are there at the end.

177
00:12:11,895 --> 00:12:16,491
通信员每周加3.5磅 登记文书每周4.2磅
?.50 a week for a messenger. ?.20 for a registry clerk.

178
00:12:16,655 --> 00:12:19,647
科技官员8.2镑 聊胜于无
?.20 for a scientific officer. Hardly anything.

179
00:12:19,815 --> 00:12:23,205
那我们每年要加26000镑?
So it would be ?6,000 a year extra for us?

180
00:12:26,335 --> 00:12:29,133
差不多吧
More or less.

181
00:12:29,295 --> 00:12:33,004
希望你没提这个吧?      亲爱的汉弗莱
You haven't mentioned that, I hope. My dear Humphrey...

182
00:12:34,095 --> 00:12:39,089
弗兰克 你不觉得这东西有被人仔细审查的危险吧?
you don't think there's a danger that someone go into detail?

183
00:12:39,255 --> 00:12:44,249
不是说它有什么错      谁会审查? 大臣只听我们的简报
Not that there's anything wrong with it. But who?

184
00:12:44,415 --> 00:12:46,975
我们都是忠诚的公务员 都想加薪
We're all loyal members of the service.

185
00:12:47,175 --> 00:12:51,771
对 我等到内阁会议当天午餐前再排到议事日程里去
Yes. I'll get it in last item before lunch on the Cabinet's agenda.

186
00:12:51,935 --> 00:12:55,848
整个议程里 他们顶多花5分钟      四平八稳
They won't spend more than 5 minutes on it. Plain sailing.

187
00:12:56,055 --> 00:13:00,048
只有韦尔斯教授会来严格审查
Apart from the rigorous scrutiny of Professor Welsh.

188
00:13:02,655 --> 00:13:05,408
首相 您首席政治顾问的电话
Your Chief Political Advisor is on the phone.

189
00:13:05,615 --> 00:13:08,493
谢谢 接过来 多萝西?
Thank you. Put her through. ..Dorothy?

190
00:13:08,695 --> 00:13:12,832
首相 我在写关于公务员加薪计划的报告
I'm doing a paper on this Civil Service pay claim,

191
00:13:12,832 --> 00:13:15,340
但我现在就得给您答复
but I can give an immediate response.

192
00:13:15,340 --> 00:13:18,929
好的 什么答复?      没有答复 是一系列问题
Yes, please. What's your answer? It's a series of questions.

193
00:13:19,135 --> 00:13:21,729
问我?      问汉弗莱爵士
For me? For Sir Humphrey.

194
00:13:21,895 --> 00:13:26,730
这份计划自私又不合时宜 很多问题有待回答
The claim is self-serving and inappropriate

195
00:13:26,935 --> 00:13:31,725
好 问吧      好 这事您应该严格保密 不然捉不住他
Right. Fire away. You should treat this as highly confidential.

196
00:13:31,895 --> 00:13:34,534
首先 您应该询问减除额标准...
First of all, you should ask what deduction...

197
00:13:36,495 --> 00:13:38,884
好...
Yes...

198
00:13:44,135 --> 00:13:46,126
太棒了
Triffic!

199
00:13:48,895 --> 00:13:54,094
乔治 这是给你的 我可以进去吧 伯纳?
All right for me to go in, Bernard?

200
00:13:54,255 --> 00:13:58,646
可以 汉弗莱爵士 我能先说件事吗?
Uh, yes. Sir Humphrey, can I just mention one thing?

201
00:13:58,815 --> 00:14:01,204
什么 伯纳?
Yes, Bernard?

202
00:14:01,375 --> 00:14:05,846
起了些变化      哪方面?
There has been movement. On what subject?

203
00:14:06,055 --> 00:14:09,650
公务员希望不起变化的那方面
On a subject we hoped for no movement.

204
00:14:09,855 --> 00:14:14,565
公务员的总体愿望是 一切方面都不起变化
The Civil Service generally hopes there will be no movement on any subject!

205
00:14:14,775 --> 00:14:19,769
对 我是说在某些通常一贯由公务员
it's in relation to a subject that is wholly and exclusively

206
00:14:19,935 --> 00:14:24,087
全权掌控的方面 展开了些进展
within the control of the Service that developments have developed.

207
00:14:24,295 --> 00:14:27,093
你在打谜语 伯纳      谢谢
You're speaking in riddles! Oh, thank you.

208
00:14:27,295 --> 00:14:31,607
这不是夸你 伯纳 拜托说清楚点
That was NOT a compliment, Bernard! Make yourself clear, please.

209
00:14:31,815 --> 00:14:34,204
很抱歉 汉弗莱爵士 我不能透露
I'm sorry, Sir Humphrey, my lips are sealed.

210
00:14:34,375 --> 00:14:39,165
我指的是我有责任记录的一次机密谈话
minutes that I was to make of a confidential conversation

211
00:14:39,335 --> 00:14:41,644
发生在首相和一名顾问之间
between the Prime Minister and an advisor.

212
00:14:41,855 --> 00:14:44,892
哪个顾问?      抱歉 我无权透露那位女士的名字
Which advisor? I cannot divulge her name.

213
00:14:45,095 --> 00:14:51,091
谢谢 伯纳 这些机密建议是关于经济危机的?
And this confidential advice was to do with the financial crisis?

214
00:14:51,295 --> 00:14:55,004
不 汉弗莱爵士 更严重      是他的蠢核武战略?
No, much more important. Not his silly nuclear strategy?

215
00:14:55,215 --> 00:15:00,130
还要严重得多      不是公务员加薪吧?
Much more important. You don't mean the Civil Service pay claim?!

216
00:15:01,375 --> 00:15:03,764
明白了 你有什么建议 伯纳?
I see. What do you advise, Bernard?

217
00:15:03,975 --> 00:15:08,969
我建议您仔细掂量您的位置 采取更加灵活的姿态
consider your position carefully, adopting a more flexible posture,

218
00:15:09,135 --> 00:15:13,925
耳朵贴地 注意动静 腿脚放灵 盯紧背后
keeping ear to the ground, covering your retreat watch your rear.

219
00:15:14,095 --> 00:15:16,848
谢谢 伯纳 你帮了大忙了
Thank you, Bernard. You've been a great help.

220
00:15:17,055 --> 00:15:19,285
实际上 汉弗莱爵士 我什么都没告诉您
Actually, I haven't told you anything.

221
00:15:19,495 --> 00:15:24,489
那当然 伯纳 太不合适了      首相 汉弗莱爵士来了
That's most improper. Prime Minister, Sir Humphrey's here.

222
00:15:25,655 --> 00:15:27,611
灵活
Flexible.

223
00:15:29,095 --> 00:15:32,690
啊 汉弗莱 进来      谢谢 首相
Ah, Humphrey! Come in. Thank you, Prime Minister.

224
00:15:32,855 --> 00:15:35,244
说说你对这个有何看法
Tell me what you think of this.

225
00:15:39,015 --> 00:15:41,210
你觉得怎样?
What do you make of it?

226
00:15:41,415 --> 00:15:46,205
这么多内容 一时很难判断      就读那一页摘要
rather large for instant judgement. read the one-page summary.

227
00:15:46,415 --> 00:15:49,885
哦 好的      怎样?
Ah. Oh, good. Well?

228
00:15:50,095 --> 00:15:51,574
怎样?
Well?

229
00:15:51,775 --> 00:15:56,166
首相 您可让我进退两难了
Prime Minister, you place me in a very difficult position.

230
00:15:56,375 --> 00:15:59,571
是吗 汉弗莱? 我知道你得忠于同僚们
Do I, Humphrey? You have to have loyalty to your colleagues

231
00:15:59,571 --> 00:16:02,207
但更重要的是 要忠于内阁及其政策
but also to Cabinet policies.

232
00:16:02,207 --> 00:16:05,567
我同意      你同意?
I agree. You agree?

233
00:16:05,775 --> 00:16:07,493
对      你同意我?
Yes. With me?

234
00:16:07,695 --> 00:16:12,325
我同意您      我...我不...你同意什么?
I agree with you. I...ah... I don't... Who do you agree with?

235
00:16:12,535 --> 00:16:15,527
同意您      不是同意弗兰克爵士?
With you. Not with Sir Frank?

236
00:16:15,695 --> 00:16:18,209
不      你不跟我争辩?
No. You're not arguing with me?

237
00:16:18,415 --> 00:16:20,212
不
No.

238
00:16:21,215 --> 00:16:23,604
也许我说得还不够清楚
Perhaps I haven't made myself quite clear.

239
00:16:23,775 --> 00:16:26,209
我同意您
I agree with you!

240
00:16:27,615 --> 00:16:30,004
那你对这个加薪计划有何看法?
Well, what do you make of that pay claim?

241
00:16:30,215 --> 00:16:32,604
这个 本身来说不算过分
Well, it's not excessive in itself,

242
00:16:32,775 --> 00:16:37,769
但值此国家危机之际 它既不明智也不符合国家利益
but at a national stringency neither wise nor in national interest.

243
00:16:37,935 --> 00:16:40,529
我不愿意批评我的同僚 可是
I don't like to criticise my colleague, but...

244
00:16:40,695 --> 00:16:45,485
我认为弗兰克爵士 尽管本意无疑是好的
though no doubt acting from the best of motives,

245
00:16:45,655 --> 00:16:50,649
应该把国家利益置于公务员的狭隘利益之上
should have placed the good of the nation before civil servants.

246
00:16:50,815 --> 00:16:53,534
您看 这份计划有些严重问题
You see, this claim raises serious questions.

247
00:16:53,735 --> 00:16:58,445
真有意思 我自己也记了几个问题
That's interesting. I've made a note of some questions, too.

248
00:16:59,495 --> 00:17:02,851
好问题 哪里来的?
Good questions. Where did they come from?

249
00:17:03,055 --> 00:17:05,444
我想到的      对
Oh, occurred to me. Yes.

250
00:17:05,655 --> 00:17:08,169
确实是...非常好的问题
They're...VERY good questions.

251
00:17:08,335 --> 00:17:11,611
对 我也这么觉得 我们拿它怎么办?
Yes, that's what I thought. What should we do?

252
00:17:11,815 --> 00:17:14,409
我们提出来      向谁提?
We should ask them. Ask who?

253
00:17:14,615 --> 00:17:18,210
向弗兰克爵士 您应该请他过来讨论
Sir Frank. You ought to invite him here to discuss them.

254
00:17:18,375 --> 00:17:22,766
他很可能知道答案 他应该知道
He may well know the answers. Indeed, he should know them.

255
00:17:22,935 --> 00:17:25,210
话说回来 这是他的职责
That's his job, after all.

256
00:17:25,415 --> 00:17:28,248
对 谢谢 汉弗莱 安排一下好吗 伯纳?
Yes. Thank you. Arrange that, Bernard.

257
00:17:28,415 --> 00:17:30,804
我得说 我非常感激你的中立 汉弗莱
I must say I appreciate your impartiality.

258
00:17:30,975 --> 00:17:34,763
如果这个通过 你的赚头也不小
You'd gain quite a lot yourself if it were to go through.

259
00:17:34,975 --> 00:17:37,364
大概是吧 首相 不过
Well, I suppose so, Prime Minister,

260
00:17:37,535 --> 00:17:42,131
坦白说 我认为这份工作的回报 就是知道
but I see the rewards of this job as the knowledge...

261
00:17:42,295 --> 00:17:47,972
我们得以造福国家 而非造福我们自己 您说呢 首相?
..that we've been of service to the nation, not to ourselves.

262
00:17:48,975 --> 00:17:53,446
我同意 谢谢 汉弗莱      谢谢您 首相
I agree. Thank you, Humphrey. Thank you, Prime Minister.

263
00:17:56,215 --> 00:18:00,128
汉弗莱真是公正 对吧?      对 首相
Humphrey's very fair-minded, isn't he? Oh, yes, Prime Minister.

264
00:18:00,895 --> 00:18:06,253
如果真有利益冲突 公务员究竟站哪边?
If there were a conflict which side are the Service really on?

265
00:18:06,455 --> 00:18:08,923
赢的那边 首相
The winning side, Prime Minister.

266
00:18:15,895 --> 00:18:21,891
谢谢 比利 我真的很痛心没能支持弗兰克
It was very painful for me not to be able to support Frank's case.

267
00:18:22,055 --> 00:18:25,047
非常令人沮丧      可他肯定会输
Deeply distressing. But he was going to lose.

268
00:18:25,215 --> 00:18:28,804
韦莱那个女人给首相列了一堆问题
And that Wainwright female had suggested

269
00:18:28,804 --> 00:18:31,259
建议不让我们处理自己的加薪计划
that they stop us handling our own pay claims

270
00:18:31,259 --> 00:18:33,614
成立一个议会特选委员会来决定
and let a Select Committee decide on them!

271
00:18:33,815 --> 00:18:38,206
太过分了 接下来政客会以失职为理由
Next thing you'd have is politicians removing civil servants

272
00:18:38,375 --> 00:18:42,493
开除公务员了 这是导火索      就是
on the grounds of incompetence! The thin end of the wedge.

273
00:18:42,695 --> 00:18:47,086
阿诺德 我需要你帮助 显然 弗兰克的计划不合适
Arnold, I need your help. Clearly, Frank's claim is discredited,

274
00:18:47,255 --> 00:18:51,646
但我必须促成加薪 才能巩固我的位置
but I need to get us the pay rise to consolidate my position.

275
00:18:51,815 --> 00:18:53,931
换你会怎么办 你做内阁秘书的时候怎么办的?
What did you do?

276
00:18:54,135 --> 00:18:58,333
你说弗兰克用了通用方案 跟工业对比?      没错
You say Frank used the normal formula? That's right.

277
00:18:58,495 --> 00:19:02,090
你需要加43%      差不多吧
And you need 43%. Hm. Thereabouts.

278
00:19:02,255 --> 00:19:06,248
既然所有相关人员实际上都在伦敦工作
Well, since virtually all the relevant staff work in London,

279
00:19:06,415 --> 00:19:11,205
首先提高伦敦津贴 津贴属于费用
start with a big increase in the London allowance. Allowances count as expenses.

280
00:19:11,375 --> 00:19:16,130
不算薪水 不计入百分比      伦敦津贴
They don't show in the percentage calculation. London allowance.

281
00:19:16,335 --> 00:19:20,931
然后施行学位特别津贴 给一等和二等甲级文凭的人
introduce a graduate allowance for Firsts and Upper Seconds.

282
00:19:21,095 --> 00:19:25,327
帮助招募新人      牛津没有二等甲级
To aid recruitment. Oxford doesn't give Upper Seconds.

283
00:19:25,535 --> 00:19:29,926
牛津的二等至少能算二等甲级
A second at Oxford counts as an Upper Second, at least.

284
00:19:30,095 --> 00:19:35,089
然后把优异功绩奖加倍 这个奖还在吧?
Then you double the Outstanding Merit awards.

285
00:19:35,295 --> 00:19:37,331
对 人人都有
Oh, yes. Everyone.

286
00:19:37,535 --> 00:19:40,811
这也不算加薪 多少了?
They don't count as rises either. Getting there?

287
00:19:41,015 --> 00:19:45,531
只剩18%要加了      从上次开始计算?
That gets us down to only about 18%. Since last time?

288
00:19:45,735 --> 00:19:50,331
别从上次算 从1973年 加薪百分比的顶峰
Then don't calculate from last time. Calculate from 1973

289
00:19:50,495 --> 00:19:56,286
也别算到今年 算到两年后 加薪阶段末期
And don't just take it to this year. Take it up to two years' time

290
00:19:56,455 --> 00:19:59,572
再考虑通货膨胀 应该够了
Correcting for inflation, that should do it.

291
00:19:59,775 --> 00:20:05,168
好极了 现在增幅显得很公正了 可还有个问题
Excellent. The percentage increases will sound all right now

292
00:20:05,335 --> 00:20:09,374
公务员薪金支出总额仍然太高
The overall Civil Service pay bill will still be too high.

293
00:20:09,575 --> 00:20:13,966
简单 缩减公务员规模      什么?
Easy. Reduce the size of the Civil Service. What?!

294
00:20:15,855 --> 00:20:21,964
如果总规模比上次小 个人合理加薪的总额就相应小了
If the service were smaller, a comfortable rise looks smaller.

295
00:20:22,175 --> 00:20:25,133
对 可是缩减公务员规模?
Real reductions in the size of the service?!

296
00:20:25,295 --> 00:20:28,970
这会是我们文明的终结
It would be the end of civilisation as we know it!

297
00:20:29,175 --> 00:20:33,566
不 亲爱的汉弗莱 你只须不再叫他们公务员
No, All you do is stop calling them civil servants.

298
00:20:33,735 --> 00:20:36,124
比如说博物馆吧
Take the museums, for instance.

299
00:20:36,295 --> 00:20:41,892
把它们改成独立基金 职员就不算公务员了
turn them into trusts, the staff stop being called civil servants.

300
00:20:42,055 --> 00:20:46,845
还是一样的人 做一样的动作 拿政府拨款
same people doing the same job and still paid by government grants,

301
00:20:47,015 --> 00:20:52,009
但拨款这东西不计入薪酬 除非有人仔细审查
but as it's a grant it doesn't count in the pay statistics.

302
00:20:52,175 --> 00:20:54,973
不然看上去就像削减
it will look like a cutback.

303
00:20:55,135 --> 00:20:57,480
能突然设立这么多基金吗?
Can we set up so many trusts in time?

304
00:20:57,480 --> 00:21:01,754
不需要 只要计划在未来两年内就行
You won't have to. It only has to be planned.

305
00:21:01,754 --> 00:21:03,969
如果最后没达成 没人会要你负责
If it doesn't happen, it won't be your fault.

306
00:21:04,135 --> 00:21:08,970
同时 你应该可以把增幅控制在6%了
you should be able to get the rise to work out at 6% overall.

307
00:21:09,175 --> 00:21:13,965
谢谢 阿诺德 多亏你了      我一向乐意帮忙
Thank you, Arnold. That's a great help. Always happy to oblige.

308
00:21:14,135 --> 00:21:17,127
尤其是生日和授勋临近的时候
Especially with the birthday honours coming up.

309
00:21:19,815 --> 00:21:22,204
要我也跟弗兰克说说吗?
Should I talk to Frank about this, too?

310
00:21:22,415 --> 00:21:27,887
不不 阿诺德 交给我吧 弗兰克问题够多了
Leave it to me. Frank's got a lot of problems coming up.

311
00:21:28,095 --> 00:21:33,044
真的?他可没提到      大概因为他还不知道吧
He hasn't mentioned them. Because he doesn't know about them yet.

312
00:21:34,975 --> 00:21:38,888
而且公务员薪酬大大落后于同等工业职务
Service pay has fallen behind comparable jobs in industry.

313
00:21:39,095 --> 00:21:41,290
什么同等职务?
What comparable jobs?

314
00:21:41,455 --> 00:21:46,085
这个比较方案很复杂 不过多年来都被普遍接受
it's quite complex but it has been accepted for some time.

315
00:21:46,295 --> 00:21:51,085
我知道常任秘书年薪超过45000镑
I understand that a Permanent Secretary earns over ?5,000 a year.

316
00:21:51,255 --> 00:21:56,283
内阁秘书和财政部常任秘书超过51000镑
Permanent Secretary to the Treasury earn in excess of ?1,000.

317
00:21:56,495 --> 00:21:58,770
也许是这样
Um...maybe you're right.

318
00:21:58,975 --> 00:22:03,685
你不知道你挣多少吗 弗兰克? 还是突然忘了?
Don't you know how much you earn or has it slipped your memory?

319
00:22:03,895 --> 00:22:06,568
对 可如果跟工业报酬比...
Yes, but if that's what industry is paying...

320
00:22:06,775 --> 00:22:10,768
你觉得呢 汉弗莱?      这不由我说 首相 我有既得利益
What do you think, Humphrey? It's not for me to say.

321
00:22:10,935 --> 00:22:13,927
弗兰克爵士负责公务员报酬 对吧弗兰克?
Sir Frank is in charge of Civil Service pay.

322
00:22:14,135 --> 00:22:17,730
首相 我能问个问题吗?      好
Prime Minister, may I ask a question? Yes.

323
00:22:17,895 --> 00:22:20,807
弗兰克爵士 你在职位保障方面的减除额是多少?
What deduction do you make for job security?

324
00:22:21,015 --> 00:22:25,611
你说什么?      工业首脑有失业之虞
I beg your pardon? Top people in industry can get sacked.

325
00:22:25,775 --> 00:22:28,573
开除 调走 公司破产 可你的职位雷打不动
They can go bust, but your jobs are guaranteed.

326
00:22:28,775 --> 00:22:32,768
有得有失嘛      什么失?
There are swings and roundabouts. What roundabouts?

327
00:22:32,935 --> 00:22:35,927
工作时间长      工业里就不长吗?
Long hours. Don't those happen in industry?

328
00:22:36,095 --> 00:22:38,973
工业首脑还得做决定
Industrial leaders must stand by decisions.

329
00:22:39,175 --> 00:22:43,487
公务员也是      真的? 不是大臣做决定嘛
So do civil servants. Really? I thought ministers took decisions.

330
00:22:43,695 --> 00:22:48,689
还担责任 是这么安排的吧?      对 大臣是得做决定
And the blame. Yes, ministers do take the decisions.

331
00:22:48,855 --> 00:22:52,006
公务员得决定如何贯彻
Civil servants must decide how to carry it out.

332
00:22:52,215 --> 00:22:55,810
就像秘书起草一封信      对
Like a secretary laying out a letter. Yes.

333
00:22:56,815 --> 00:22:59,773
不 汉弗莱爵士明白我的意思
No! Um... Sir Humphrey knows what I mean.

334
00:22:59,975 --> 00:23:04,332
得由你说 弗兰克 你负责公务员报酬
It's up to you, Frank. You're in charge of Civil Service pay.

335
00:23:05,695 --> 00:23:08,812
那公益服务成份呢?
What about the service element?

336
00:23:09,015 --> 00:23:11,483
公益服务成份? 什么意思?
Service element? What do you mean?

337
00:23:17,095 --> 00:23:20,974
这份工作有很强的公益性      可不是
The job has a strong element of service. Absolutely.

338
00:23:21,175 --> 00:23:25,566
报酬是巴思爵士 二等勋爵士 骑士勋位 弗兰克爵士
Rewarded by CBs and KCMGs and knighthoods...Sir Frank.

339
00:23:25,775 --> 00:23:27,811
从某种意义上说
To an extent.

340
00:23:28,015 --> 00:23:32,805
首相 也许我们更应该把公务员比作慈善机构董事
shouldn't compare civil servants with directors of charities

341
00:23:32,975 --> 00:23:37,969
而不是工业董事 他们平均年薪17000镑 不是45000
rather than industries. They get ?7,000 a year on average

342
00:23:38,135 --> 00:23:42,925
这个提议有意思      不 我认为...那我们永远招不到人了
That's an interesting proposal. We'd never recruit.

343
00:23:43,095 --> 00:23:47,008
士气会直线下降 汉弗莱爵士肯定同意
Morale would plummet. I'm sure Sir Humphrey would agree.

344
00:23:47,215 --> 00:23:50,605
汉弗莱?      我的意见是
Humphrey? Well, it's my opinion that...

345
00:23:50,775 --> 00:23:53,369
弗兰克爵士负责公务员报酬
..Sir Frank is in charge of Civil Service pay.

346
00:23:53,535 --> 00:23:58,529
我认为首相完全有权得到答复 弗兰克
I do think the Prime Minister is entitled to an answer, Frank.

347
00:23:58,735 --> 00:24:04,810
还有物价指数化退休金问题      对 这个早就有共识了
Then there are indexed pensions. those were agreed a long time ago.

348
00:24:05,015 --> 00:24:09,008
价值非常大 对吧      价值 对 可并不过分
They're of considerable value. Of value, yes, but modest.

349
00:24:09,175 --> 00:24:15,125
这份估价说 买断一位常任秘书的退休金要65万镑
it would cost ?50,000 to buy back a Permanent Secretary's pension.

350
00:24:15,335 --> 00:24:17,610
荒谬      你估计呢?
Absurd. How do you value it?

351
00:24:17,815 --> 00:24:22,411
大约10万磅      那好 我们做个交易 弗兰克
Er, about ?00,000. In that case, I'll make you a deal, Frank.

352
00:24:22,575 --> 00:24:27,365
由政府买断你的退休金 别人乐意出售也行
The government will buy back your pension 

353
00:24:27,535 --> 00:24:33,132
就照你的估价 我们给你10万磅现金 好吗?
at your own valuation. 100,000 in cash for your pension rights?

354
00:24:33,335 --> 00:24:39,126
我说的是...就是随口一说 不可能...
I was talking out of my...off the top of my head.

355
00:24:39,295 --> 00:24:41,570
我自己也没算过
I haven't calculated it myself.

356
00:24:41,775 --> 00:24:46,405
65万这个数字来自保险和退休金精算协会
The figure of ?50,000 comes from the Society of Insurance

357
00:24:46,615 --> 00:24:51,450
对 可当初达成的共识肯定不是这样
Yes, but when it was agreed I'm sure it was nothing like that.

358
00:24:51,655 --> 00:24:56,445
这个主意怎样? 物价指数化退休金和勋位平行
An indexed pension could be an alternative to honours.

359
00:24:56,615 --> 00:25:01,245
每位公务员自行选择 要勋位还是钱
Every civil servant could choose honours or cash.

360
00:25:01,455 --> 00:25:03,764
无稽之谈     为什么?
That's preposterous! Why?

361
00:25:03,975 --> 00:25:07,934
对啊 为什么?      这个 它 它...
Yes, why? Well, it, it, it, it, it...

362
00:25:08,095 --> 00:25:13,215
它会让我们...让他们很为难的 有些已经有勋位了
It would put us put THEM in an impossible position.

363
00:25:13,415 --> 00:25:18,205
简单 他们可以选择放弃勋位还是放弃钱
They could choose whether to renounce their honour or pension

364
00:25:18,375 --> 00:25:23,369
你觉得呢 汉弗莱爵士? 或者阿普比先生?
What do you think, Sir Humphrey? Or will you be Mr Appleby?

365
00:25:24,495 --> 00:25:28,966
我肯定弗兰克爵士已经彻底考虑过了
I'm sure that Sir Frank has gone into this very thoroughly.

366
00:25:29,175 --> 00:25:33,851
还不够彻底 你自己也会赚到不少 对吧?
Not thoroughly enough. You'd stand to gain quite a lot personally.

367
00:25:34,055 --> 00:25:36,808
首相 这不列入考虑
Prime Minister, that is not a consideration.

368
00:25:37,015 --> 00:25:40,894
你乐意你个人被剔除出这次加薪?
You'd be happy to be personally excluded from this rise?

369
00:25:41,095 --> 00:25:44,087
我知道内阁秘书肯定乐意 是吧汉弗莱?
I know the Cabinet Secretary would be.

370
00:25:44,255 --> 00:25:49,454
当然 问题是...本质上 这种先例...
Well, of course, the question is... not as a precedent...

371
00:25:49,615 --> 00:25:52,209
通盘考虑整个公务员系统...
..thinking of the service as a whole...

372
00:25:52,375 --> 00:25:57,574
从 从长远角度来说 原则上要求...
from the long-term point of view... as a matter of principle...

373
00:25:59,495 --> 00:26:03,693
说呀      当然
Go on. Well, of course...

374
00:26:03,855 --> 00:26:05,652
如果...
..IF...

375
00:26:05,815 --> 00:26:08,807
如果...政府真的相信
..if...the government did believe

376
00:26:08,975 --> 00:26:12,968
高阶人员应该比下属拿得少
that senior people should be paid less than their subordinates,

377
00:26:13,135 --> 00:26:17,731
如果这一原则延伸到内阁大臣和新晋大臣
and if the principle were extended to Cabinet ministers

378
00:26:17,935 --> 00:26:21,450
总之 弗兰克 多谢你过来
Anyway, Frank, thank you very much for coming in.

379
00:26:21,655 --> 00:26:24,453
谢谢您 首相
Thank you, Prime Minister.

380
00:26:28,495 --> 00:26:33,888
你觉得怎样 有点苛刻吧?      不 非常合适而有见地的问题
A bit hard? No. Most proper and penetrating questions.

381
00:26:34,055 --> 00:26:37,047
现在怎么办?      我想跟您私下说一句
What happens now? I'd like a word in private.

382
00:26:37,215 --> 00:26:40,412
我正要走      好 多萝西
I was just going. Good.

383
00:26:40,615 --> 00:26:43,209
真是太感谢你了      亲爱(珍贵)的女士
Thank you very much indeed. Dear lady.

384
00:26:43,375 --> 00:26:46,572
可比不上内阁秘书贵 汉弗莱
Not as dear as a Cabinet Secretary, Humphrey.

385
00:26:46,775 --> 00:26:53,089
首相 我真的很难着手 我痛恨对同僚不忠诚
One does so hate to be disloyal to one's colleagues.

386
00:26:53,295 --> 00:26:56,287
显然你没当过内阁大臣
Clearly you've never been a Cabinet minister!

387
00:26:56,455 --> 00:27:01,245
我一直都觉得 在这种紧张时期 财政部的要求太过分了
I'd felt all along, at a time of stringency, that the Treasury claim was too high.

388
00:27:01,415 --> 00:27:03,804
不符合国家利益 对公务员当然非常好
Not in the nation's interests. Very nice for us,

389
00:27:03,975 --> 00:27:08,969
但一位高度忠诚的内阁秘书很难苟同
but not something the Cabinet Secretary could recommend.

390
00:27:09,135 --> 00:27:14,528
这就是为什么我们不让财政部常任秘书统领公务员
It's why we don't let the Treasury be head of the Civil Service.

391
00:27:14,695 --> 00:27:19,291
所以我擅自拟定了一份低调得多的计划
So I've drawing up a much more modest submission

392
00:27:19,455 --> 00:27:24,245
未来两年内增加11% 高阶人员仅高于平均数
only 11% over two years with the top grades rising the average

393
00:27:24,415 --> 00:27:30,092
其间公务员薪酬支出总额每年只增加6%
and the overall Civil Service pay bill going up by only 6%

394
00:27:30,295 --> 00:27:32,445
这看上去合理多了
This looks much more reasonable.

395
00:27:32,655 --> 00:27:37,251
对 当然 低阶人员加薪还得经过正常程序
Yes. The lower grades will have to go through the normal procedures,

396
00:27:37,415 --> 00:27:41,727
但我建议高阶人员方面应该立即秘密推行
but the First Division should be processed with secrecy.

397
00:27:41,935 --> 00:27:45,325
秘密 为什么?      如果发起广泛讨论
Secrecy? Why? If there were widespread discussion,

398
00:27:45,535 --> 00:27:50,325
也许会适得其反 我们有些人也许要提出高得多的计划
Some of our people might want to put in a much bigger claim.

399
00:27:50,495 --> 00:27:53,089
造成既成事实比较好
Much better to present a fait accompli.

400
00:27:53,255 --> 00:27:58,090
我建议能否避免...让顾问过目?
And may I advise against letting...advisors see it?

401
00:27:59,095 --> 00:28:02,167
你的同僚真能接受只加6%吗?
Are you sure your colleagues would accept 6%?

402
00:28:02,375 --> 00:28:05,367
如果有您的支持与合作 能的
If I had your support and co-operation, yes.

403
00:28:05,575 --> 00:28:10,968
那还是得议会批准 后座议员痛恨公务员加薪
It's still get through Parliament. They hate Service pay rises.

404
00:28:11,175 --> 00:28:13,564
您提到这点真是太巧了
Oh! How interesting you should say that!

405
00:28:13,735 --> 00:28:18,126
我刚要提个建议 一项重大改革      好
I was just about to make a suggestion, a major reform.

406
00:28:18,295 --> 00:28:23,289
首相 如果把议员的薪酬跟同级公务员挂钩
MPs' salaries were to be linked to a grade in the Civil Service,

407
00:28:23,455 --> 00:28:27,448
他们就不用总投票给自己加薪了
they wouldn't need to vote themselves pay rises all the time.

408
00:28:27,615 --> 00:28:30,607
只要公务员加 他们自动也加
If the Civil Service got one, they'd get one.

409
00:28:30,775 --> 00:28:33,573
如果议员的退休金也物价指数化
And if MPs' pensions were index-linked,

410
00:28:33,735 --> 00:28:37,648
他们对公务员薪酬的敌意会大大缓和的
it would make them much less hostile to Civil Service pay claims.

411
00:28:37,855 --> 00:28:40,653
肯定会 太妙了
It certainly would. Excellent.

412
00:28:40,815 --> 00:28:43,807
谢谢 汉弗莱      首相
Thank you, Humphrey. Prime Minister.

413
00:28:43,975 --> 00:28:46,330
后座议员跟哪级挂钩?
What grade ought backbenchers be?

414
00:28:46,535 --> 00:28:50,528
资深主任吧?      级别太低了吧?
Senior Principals. Isn't that rather low?

415
00:28:50,695 --> 00:28:53,004
后座议员本来就低级
Backbenchers are rather low.

416
00:28:53,215 --> 00:28:57,606
那内阁大臣呢?      副秘书长?
And what grade for Cabinet ministers? Under Secretaries.

417
00:28:57,775 --> 00:29:00,005
首相呢?
And the Prime Minister?

418
00:29:00,215 --> 00:29:04,208
这个嘛 眼下 您的薪水比我还低
Well, at the moment, you earn even less than I do.

419
00:29:04,375 --> 00:29:09,165
何不把您自己与算作常任秘书呢?
Why don't you grade yourself as a Permanent Secretary?

420
00:29:09,335 --> 00:29:13,647
谢谢 汉弗莱      话说回来 我们是合伙关系
Thank you, Humphrey. After all, this is a partnership.

421
00:29:13,855 --> 00:29:18,645
对 真正的合伙关系      是 首相
Yes. A real partnership. Yes, Prime Minister.

422
00:29:19,460 --> 00:29:29,570
